From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haseenesss <Haseenesss@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 19:12:35 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] host/input: box DM_GAME_ID for the Mac preferences domain

input_preferences_domain() joined @"org.nxnative." and DM_GAME_ID as two
string literals. A multi-program profile (Super Mario 3D All-Stars,
010049900F546000) defines DM_GAME_ID as (dm_game_cur()->id), a runtime
const char *, so front_mac.m and controllers_mac.m failed to compile
and the Mac host could not be built. The ID is now boxed at run time,
as front_mac.m already does with @(DM_GAME_ID). seedds/nxnative#221's
branch has the same line since; patch 0017 was adapted before it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#221 (the fix is on that pull request's branch; patch 0017 predates it)
Reason: a multi-program game's Mac host does not compile: patch 0017 joins a runtime DM_GAME_ID as a string literal
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#1145

---
 dm/host/input_preferences_mac.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dm/host/input_preferences_mac.h b/dm/host/input_preferences_mac.h
index b3a2dee..bedb78a 100644
--- a/dm/host/input_preferences_mac.h
+++ b/dm/host/input_preferences_mac.h
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 #include "game_profile.h"
 #include "input_map.h"
 static NSString *input_preferences_domain(void) {
-    return NSBundle.mainBundle.bundleIdentifier ?: [@"org.nxnative." DM_GAME_ID lowercaseString];
+    return NSBundle.mainBundle.bundleIdentifier ?: [[@"org.nxnative." stringByAppendingString:@(DM_GAME_ID)] lowercaseString];
 }
 static BOOL input_preferences_enabled(void) {
     const char *off=getenv("DM_SAVED_CHOICES"); return !off || strcmp(off,"0");
